\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces HJ-Biplot of TAM questionnaire responses ($n{=}25$). Dimension~1 explains 43.6\,\% of variance; Dimension~2 explains 24.2\,\%~(cumulative: 67.8\,\%). Arrows indicate item vectors; proximity of participant points to a vector reflects agreement with that item. The PU cluster (PTAM001--006) and most PEOU items (PTAM008--010) point in the same direction, indicating high internal correlation. PTAM007 and PTAM012 are orthogonal to the main cluster, capturing independent variance.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
